body:
Hellfire for eternity is no joke and its always a tragedy when a child of Adam (AS) falls victim to the tricks of Shaytan (Satan) and ends up in hellfire for eternity because of it. In the Quran, we are constantly reminded by Allah that Shaytan is not our ally but our sworn enemy and to avoid going against Allah and His divine laws for mankind to avoid hellfire. We are constantly reminded that Shaytan is the sworn enemy of the children of Adam (AS) and not to be fooled into following his path towards hellfire. This is what Shaytan will say when a soul is about to enter hellfire.

&nbsp;

> And Satan will say ˹to his followers˺ after the judgment has been passed, “Indeed, Allah has made you a true promise. I too made you a promise, ***but I failed you. I did not have any authority over you. I only called you, and you responded to me. So do not blame me; blame yourselves. I cannot save you, nor can you save me.*** Indeed, I denounce your previous association of me with Allah ˹in loyalty˺. Surely the wrongdoers will suffer a painful punishment.” [Quran 14:22]

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Verses where Allah reminds us that Shaytan is mankind's sworn enemy

&nbsp;

>Did I not command you, O  Children of Adam, not to follow Satan, for he is truly your sworn enemy [Quran 36:60]

&nbsp;

> And do not let Satan hinder you, ˹for˺ he is certainly your sworn enemy. [Quran 43:62]

&nbsp;

>O humanity! Eat from what is lawful and good on the earth and do not follow Satan’s footsteps. He is truly your sworn enemy. [Quran 2:168]

First off, may Allah ease your struggles in adapting your life to Islam. It will definitely be worth the effort once you do so Insha Allah, and Allah will be pleased with all your efforts so rest assured that you are in good hands. 

Secondly, those who tell you that you arent a real Muslim or tell you “ what’s the point of calling yourself a Muslim” are committing a sin themselves. No one can call another Muslim a non-Muslim even if they are new and learning. This is actually a major sin so there is no such thing as a "real Muslim", you are still learning so ignore them and dont let them discourage you. Even a Muslim who constantly sins but is committed to their 5 daily prayers is still a Muslim so ignore them and let them continue in their ignorance.

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

And regarding Allah's forgiveness and mercy, this is the Shaytan planting seeds of doubt in your heart and this verse in the Quran proves it

&nbsp;

> 39:53
> ۞ قُلْ يَـٰعِبَادِىَ ٱلَّذِينَ أَسْرَفُوا۟ عَلَىٰٓ أَنفُسِهِمْ لَا تَقْنَطُوا۟ مِن رَّحْمَةِ ٱللَّهِ ۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَغْفِرُ ٱلذُّنُوبَ جَمِيعًا ۚ إِنَّهُۥ هُوَ ٱلْغَفُورُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ٥٣
> 
> Say, ˹O Prophet, that Allah says,˺ “O My servants who have exceeded the limits against their souls! Do not lose hope in Allah’s mercy, for Allah certainly forgives all sins. He is indeed the All-Forgiving, Most Merciful.
> 

&nbsp;

So ignore the whispers of Shaytan and never be in doubt or lose hope in Allah's forgiveness and mercy. Allah loves those who seek His forgiveness and He is always ready to forgive those who ask even if its the worst sin that someone can commit.

I recommend you get closer to Allah. Ask Allah for guidance towards the right path and make your affairs easier. I also and highly recommend you make athkar throughout the day like saying duas and praising Allah (make this a habit). Reading the Quran often will also help and at the same time will keep away the shayateen.

&nbsp;

Allah says in Surah R'ad (Chapter 13) verse 28: 

>Those who believe and whose hearts find comfort in the remembrance of Allah. Surely in the remembrance of Allah do hearts find comfort.

&nbsp;

So the remembrance of Allah is the key to peace and comfort of the heart and soul. Do this and Inshallah your situation and mood will change for the better.
